we're here when the quarterbacks and the  other players are here justin herbert  out of the blue plops down had a nice  conversation with him following our  extended  uh excerpts from the joe burrow press  conference we try to get joe burrow he's  not doing anything other than the podium  right i i spoke to his people last week  they're doing nothing other than the  podium and you know he's the guy who's  got the hay in the barn at the top of  the process why do anything more he had  done some media  and there was some stuff that didn't  necessarily harmonize about what the  plan is and what the preferences are as  it relates to the cincinnati bengals he  addressed some of that today he was  asked about playing for the bengals if  drafted by the bengals he said well i'm  not going to not show up joe burrow  right now  i'm not going to not show up right i'm  still going to do i thought he wasn't  doing media i'm stuck they told me he  wasn't doing meetings maybe it's  something  because we were the ones who had  really been  pointing out the discrepancy between  things he had said things that carson  palmer said things that joe burrows said  to dan patrick he said that you want to  be the first overall pick but you want  to play for a team that is committed to  winning that came just days after carson  palmer had said the bengals aren't  committed to winning he seemed to put a  lot of that to rest as it relates to his  willingness to submit to the process and  i've seen some people  on social media who are reporters who i  would think know better than what they  have said right for joe burrow to come  out at his press conference and say  i'm going to submit to the process i'm  going to play for whoever picks me that  doesn't mean he wants to play for a  given team sure he's just accepted the  fact that he has to go wherever he's  picked because what's the alternative  you know if you're the first overall  pick you're not going to say no to 36  million dollars over four years fully  guaranteed you're going to go there that  doesn't mean in his heart that he's not  maybe hoping right that it works out a  different way right that's two different  things all together yeah well and either  way i thought he handled this press  conference you know very very well he's  phenomenal in those settings he really  is and that's he's going to check all  the boxes off the field along with  checking just about everyone on the  field too and that's what's going to  make him the slam dunk number one pick  i'm glad he answered it the way he did  you know you know he even tried to say  you know the one reason i didn't just  come out definitively and say oh yeah i  want to play for them he goes i didn't  want to sound presumptuous like i  definitely was going to be the number  one pick so i think at least he  silenced some of the murmurs now we're  going to get more of a feel for this as  we continue to go on too because we'll  hear you know after he meets after the  combine and his representatives get to  meet with the bengals and there starts  to get conversations we'll start to hear  some of the rumors about how comfortable  maybe he is with the bangles and so on  and we'll see where it goes from there  and that's the art here you can't come  out and say unless you're prepared to  see it through and sit out if need be  right you can't come out and say i'm not  going to play for the team that drafts  me and quarterbacks really do have  leverage i was intrigued by one of his  comments he was asked about when he said  last week that he has leverage he said  he was talking about the scouting  combine and working out and he's not  going to work out this week well that's  really not leveraging right as it  relates to the process right you don't  work out a lot of guys don't work out  that's not an exercise of leverage  that's a personal choice  i just i personally believe and i think  one of the frankly one of the reasons he  may not be sitting here with us is he's  going to face questions like this from  us if he was here  i think deep down there is a concern  that he knows there's nothing he can do  anything about for now he can't do  anything about it especially for now and  ultimately he can't do anything about it  other than maybe hope that you can plant  a seed of doubt in the team that has the  first overall picks mind that maybe it's  not in their best interest to bring a  guy who may not be all in because you  need your quarterback to be all in we  talked about that earlier in the show  yeah he needs to show up early stay late  be a leader hold people accountable he  has to want to be there and be the  leader of that team if he's reluctant  it's not going to work for anybody and  that may be the message that based upon  what he sees and hears and learns he may  send in subtle or not so subtle fashion  to the bengals if it comes to that so i  guess my broader point is this what he  said today doesn't matter it does not  end this question whether he hopes deep  down right they don't take him that is  not resolved and anybody who says it is  wrong i can understand bengals fans  sanded people in the media who i would  like to think are smart enough to  understand the distinction some of them  aren't aren't seeing it whether they're  doing that on purpose to pander to  bengals fans or not is a different issue  but there are two different questions  here yeah there is two different  questions you know at the very least you  can be impressed by what we saw there um  this has a lot of story left to be  written here certainly  um i think what also plays into the  angle is something you've mentioned a  lot the fact that he's working with you  know carson palmer's brother and uh  carson palmer of course did not have a  great marriage with the cincinnati  bengals i think that leads us to more  questions because we think that the  palmer family is probably telling joe  burrow more the dysfunctional things  that went on in the bengals organization  that maybe we're not aware of but of  course carson palmer is so those are the  things that we're going to see going  forward and yeah i think this is still a  very  early in this process and this will be  the first chance for zach taylor to sell  himself uh to  to joe burrow to say listen like there's  something to be excited about i know  offensive football i'm a young guy we'll  grow together and you know kick some  butt together that way too and whether  joe burrow and his camp buys it or that  yet that's and i'm glad you put it that  way yeah because we are conditioned to  believe and we just had a kid here  justin herbert on set who talked about  what an honor it is to be here justin  it's not an honor to be here they see  value in these guys they see benefit  they see the potential to make a lot of  money and win a lot of football games  with these players justin herbert has  earned this honor this is not an honor  per se it's a job interview where there  needs to be more of the teams selling  themselves to the players than it than  the players selling themselves to the  team especially for the guys who have  leverage as joe burrow said the guy if  it's a quarterback and he's not all in  you got to sell yourself to him to get  him to be all in with your team well  that's part of what the bengals need to  do you're right all right so you go  through the draft though how many guys  really have leverage like i look at it  right now i just really really want to  say like the only those are the only two  guys right chase young and joe has some  just from the standpoint if you're a  quarterback if you're a high first round  quarterback yeah and you don't want to  be with the team  and they get the impression you don't  want to be with the team that's a  problem yeah so those guys have leverage  but you have to use it in subtle ways  and i think that's may that may be why  burrow said what he said look yeah yeah  i think maybe the the horse started to  get a little too far  out of the barn or the cart got in front  of the horse or whatever stupid cliche  i'm trying to say right i think that  there's a subtlety and a nuance to  pulling this off to get a team to not  draft you and it became too big of a  story and it's really not all that  complicated he says i'll play for  whoever picks me carson palmer says the  bengals aren't committed to winning he  hires jordan palmer to  coach him and then he tells dan patrick  i want to be the number one overall pick  but  i want to play for a team that's  committed to winning yeah right those  full circles pretty clearly those  questions are two different answers  today doesn't change  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

